From: Marionette AirDrop driver research
Subject: [EXPERIMENTAL] stop mission timer before clearing monitor vdev

The monitor reset path clears mon_pdev->mvdev before asynchronous WMA/SME
teardown. Stop the MSI polling timer before that clear and outside mon_lock,
so a callback cannot retain a stale monitor vdev or deadlock on the lock.
The callback rearm guard from 0030 remains a second race defense. No packet
format, firmware, or TX behavior changes.

--- a/qca-wifi-host-cmn/dp/wifi3.0/monitor/dp_mon.c
+++ b/qca-wifi-host-cmn/dp/wifi3.0/monitor/dp_mon.c
@@ -217,6 +217,12 @@
 
 	if (!pdev)
 		return QDF_STATUS_E_FAILURE;
+
+	/* Stop the mission MSI polling timer before clearing mvdev or entering
+	 * asynchronous WMA/SME teardown. This call is deliberately outside the
+	 * monitor lock: timer callback work may need that lock to drain. */
+	if (soc->intr_mode == DP_INTR_MSI)
+		dp_monitor_vdev_timer_stop(soc);
 
 	mon_pdev = pdev->monitor_pdev;
 
